Run associated tests, or explicit --test selections, against exactly one
--component or --image. Selectors accept test names and test-group names.

Reuse local subject artifacts, building when missing; --rebuild forces a build,
--artifact-source lkg selects published artifacts, and --rpm/--image-path supply
explicit component/image inputs. Component supporting images default independently
to published LKG; use --base-image-source local or --base-image-path to override.
Component selection does not require packaging lock consistency.

TMT supports VM, container, SSH, and host component tests; image tests support VM
and container. LISA uses VMs, and pytest inspects artifacts on the host. Host/SSH
execution may modify the target: use designated disposable test systems.

Results and native logs remain under the test work directory. --junit-xml writes
an aggregate report. All selected tests run unless --fail-fast is set. The older
'component test NAME' and 'image test NAME' commands remain supported.

Usage:
  azldev test run [flags]

Examples:
  azldev test run --component curl --base-image vm-base
  azldev test run --component curl --rpm ./curl.rpm --base-image-path ./base.qcow2
  azldev test run --image vm-base --image-path ./candidate.qcow2 --test smoke
  azldev test run --image vm-base --artifact-source lkg

Flags:
      --arch string                Target architecture: x86_64 or aarch64 (defaults to host)
      --artifact-source string     Subject artifact source: local (default; reuse or build), lkg, or path
      --base-image string          Named supporting image for component tests (defaults from test/distro configuration)
      --base-image-path string     Explicit supporting VM image or OCI archive path
      --base-image-source string   Supporting image source: lkg (default), local, or path
      --component string           Component name
      --execution string           Execution strategy: vm, container, ssh, or host (framework default when omitted)
      --fail-fast                  Stop starting tests after the first failure
  -h, --help                       help for run
      --image string               Image name (project definition or published catalog)
  -i, --image-path string          Explicit image under test; overrides local build selection
      --junit-xml string           Write an aggregated JUnit XML report for all selected tests
      --lisa-dir string            Local LISA framework checkout instead of cloning
      --plan string                TMT plan override
      --rebuild                    Rebuild the subject locally instead of reusing existing output
      --rebuild-base-image         Build the named supporting image locally
  -r, --rpm strings                Explicit binary RPM paths/globs for a component; overrides the complete component build
      --source-dir string          Local test source override instead of cloning (TMT/pytest)
      --ssh-host string            Existing SSH target hostname (--execution ssh)
      --ssh-key string             Private key for the existing SSH target
      --ssh-port int               Existing SSH target port (defaults to 22)
      --ssh-user string            Existing SSH target username
  -t, --test strings               Test or test-group name (repeatable; defaults to associated tests)
      --work-dir string            Root for isolated test runs (defaults to the project work directory)

Global Flags:
  -y, --accept-all                accept all prompts
      --color mode                output colorization mode {always, auto, never} (default auto)
      --concurrency int           base concurrency limit (default: number of logical CPUs; minimum 1)
      --config-file stringArray   additional TOML config file(s) to merge (may be repeated)
  -n, --dry-run                   dry run only (do not take action)
      --network-retries int       maximum number of attempts for network operations (minimum 1) (default 3)
      --no-default-config         disable default configuration
  -O, --output-format fmt         output format {csv, json, markdown, table} (default table)
      --permissive-config         do not fail on unknown fields in TOML config files
  -C, --project string            path to Azure Linux project
  -q, --quiet                     only enable minimal output
  -v, --verbose                   enable verbose output
      --without-lockfile          preview: track resolved upstream commits in generated config instead of lock files

